#basePath	Day1

:: OpeningCutscene
@trigger SceneReady
@cutscene
@who    IntroCutscene

$call InitUpdateMasks()
$call SetInstrumentUnlocked(CoordinateInstrument, true)
$call SetInstrumentUnlocked(PhotometerInstrument, true)
$call SetInputState(false)
$call StopPuzzleMode()
$call StopOpenMode()
$call SetRefGuidePagesLocked(true)

$call PlayMusic("Music.Gently-Falling", 1)
$call IntroCutscene->BeginCutscene()
$call Wait(2)
$call TelescopeLook(155, -30)

:: ArrivalAtTheShed
@trigger    CutsceneEnd
@when cutsceneId == "IntroCutscene"
@cutscene
@who    Radio

{@Astrid} Whoa. This place has really changed. Elijah, where are you? $[Astrid/L1/l1_a_01]
$call SubtitleController->SetSubtitlePosition(0.5, 0, 0, 40)
$call Wait(1)

$call MoveToView("Right")
{@Radio} CERES HQ to Station Twelve. Elijah, do you copy? Please log in and provide status report.
{@Astrid} Oh, a radio signal! How do I work this thing? Hello? This is Astrid... Elijah's friend. $[Astrid/L1/l1_a_02]
{@Radio} Station Twelve, please log in and report.
{@Astrid} Log in? How exactly am I supposed to do that? $[Astrid/L1/l1_a_03]

{@Dad} I told you, he's not there... Astrid? Is that you? $[Day1/Dad/l1_d_1]

{@Astrid} (*gasp*) Dad! I- I can’t believe it's you. Are you still at the South Pole? Can you hear me? $[Astrid/L1/l1_a_04]

{@Dad} Loud and clear...Well . . . not clear, exactly. But you know what I mean.
{@Dad} It’s so good to hear your voice, Little Bear.

{@Astrid} Do you know where Elijah is? I came here looking for him. $[Astrid/L1/l1_a_05]

{@Dad} I’m sorry, Astrid . . . I wish I could’ve warned you in time. Elijah’s not there. He probably won’t be back for a while.

{@Astrid} What? Why not? Where is he? $[Astrid/L1/l1_a_06]

{@Dad} It’s sort of a long story.
{@Dad} My team here at IceCube is working to rebuild our knowledge of the cosmos, everything that was lost during the collapse. 
{@Dad} Elijah’s been helping us. But a few weeks ago he reached out about something big he’d been working on. 
{@Dad} He said he was heading out to visit the other stations. I haven’t heard from him in awhile - you know him, always hard to pin down
{@Dad} I haven’t heard from him in awhile - you know him, always hard to pin down

{@Astrid} Wait a second. He’s been working with you? $[Astrid/L1/l1_a_07]

{@Monitor} All Ceres transmissions must comply with authorized protocols, or we’ll be forced to revoke your clearance. 
{@Monitor} This is an official warning.
{@Monitor} Remember, communication is a privilege, not a right.

{@Astrid} Whoa. Who was that? $[Astrid/L1/l1_a_08]

{@Dad} Sorry, uh…“Station Twelve,” this channel doesn’t allow for… personal communications. 
{@Dad} I’ll grant you entry-level access so you can help us. I should sign off now. More later.

$call Wait(1)

{@Radio} Station 12, this is CERES HQ. You have been granted entry level access.
{@Radio} Training begins immediately. Please follow all directives.

{@Astrid} Um, okay... Gosh, there’s a lot of buttons here... $[Astrid/L1/l1_a_09]
$call WaitForMovedToView("Monitor")

{@Radio} I'll help you get up and running. Start by moving your telescope.

$call StartMonitorControls()
$call SetInputState(true)
$call HintModals->SlideInFromRight("TelescopeControls", 0.4)
$set temp:introMoveTheTelescope = false
$branch .MoveTelescopeReminder

:: MoveTelescopeReminder
$call Wait(10)
$if !temp:introMoveTheTelescope
    {@Radio} See if you can move your telescope.
    $goto .MoveTelescopeReminder
$endif
// //TODO Shake UI hint

:: MoveYourTelescope
@trigger    OnTelescopeMoved
@when   !temp:introMoveTheTelescope
@boostScore 100
@interrupt
@cutscene
@once

$set temp:introMoveTheTelescope = true
$call HintModals->Hide("TelescopeControls", 0.2)

$call SetInputState(false)
{@Radio} Your equipment seems to be working. Let’s test it out and look for the constellation Ursa Major. Sending coordinates now…
$call MonitorUI->PlayRadioDownload(4.0)
OK, looks like you received the coordinates. See those dots above your monitor? They will light up as you near the target.
$call SetInputState(true)

$call StartNeutrinoNavigation()
$call HintModals->SlideInFromLeft("NeutrinoNav", 0.4)

:: DadHotColdEncouragement1
@trigger    OnNeutrinoNavWarmer
@when   newPips == 1
@once

{@Radio} Nice! Getting warmer...

:: DadHotColdEncouragement2
@trigger    OnNeutrinoNavWarmer
@when   newPips == 3
@once

{@Radio} Waaaaarrrrrmmmmmmeeerrrr!

:: DadColder
@trigger    OnNeutrinoNavColder
@when   newPips == 1

{@Radio} Colder...


:: NeutrinoNavigationComplete
@trigger    NeutrinoNavigationComplete
@boostScore 100
@cutscene
@once
@interrupt

$call StopNeutrinoNavigation()
$call SetInputState(false)
$call AlignCamToNeutrino()
$call HintModals->Hide("NeutrinoNav", 0.2)
$call SetInputState(false)
$call StartOpenMode()
{@Radio} Nice Job! 
$call Wait(1)
{@Radio} So earlier this morning, Ice Cube detected a high energy neutrino coming from one of several possible stars in this location.
{@Radio} You’ll see each of them highlighted on your display. 
{@Radio} Identifying these stars will be a great way for you to get your feet wet and upgrade your access level.
{@Radio} Alight. Select a possible neutrino origin on your display.
$set temp:waitingForNeutrinoStar = true

$call HintModals->SlideInFromLeft("SelectStar", 0.4)
$call SetInputState(true)

:: OnStarSelected
@trigger    OnStarSelected
@when   temp:waitingForNeutrinoStar
@cutscene
@interrupt

{@Radio} Hmmm. It doesn't look like that is a possible neutrino origin. Look for objects with a blue highlight.

:: OnRefGuideClosed
@trigger    OnRefGuideClosed
@boostScore 300
@interrupt

$set temp:guideOpen = false

:: IntroRefGuideOpened
@trigger    OnRefGuideOpened
@when   temp:waitingForManualOpen
@boostScore 300
@interrupt
@cutscene
@once

$set temp:waitingForManualOpen = false
$call SetInputState(false)
$call SubtitleController->SetSubtitlePosition(0.5, 1, 0, -140)
$call MoveToView("Right")
{@Radio} Do you see your photometer in the equipment stack? That should tell you what the apparent magnitude of the star.
{@Radio} All you need to do is find that number in your reference guide and submit the data.
$call SetInputState(true)
$call Wait(1)
$call SubtitleController->SetSubtitlePosition(0.5, 0, 0, 40)

:: OnRefGuideOpened
@trigger    OnRefGuideOpened
@interrupt

$set temp:guideOpen = true

:: OnNeutrinoStarSelected
@trigger    OnNeutrinoStarSelected
@when   temp:waitingForNeutrinoStar
@boostScore 100
@interrupt
@cutscene
@once

$set temp:waitingForNeutrinoStar = false
$set temp:waitingForManualOpen = true
$call HintModals->Hide("SelectStar", 0.2)
$call SubtitleController->SetSubtitlePosition(0.5, 0, 0, 650)

$if temp:guideOpen
    $goto .IntroRefGuideOpened
$endif

{@Radio} Great! See if you can find Elijah’s operator manual. It's a small, spiral bound notebook.
$call Wait(1)
$call SubtitleController->SetSubtitlePosition(0.5, 0, 0, 40)

:: PlayerLeavesNeutrinoTask
@trigger    OnLeaveNeutrinoRegion
@once

{@Radio} You are headed off target.

:: PlayerLeavesNeutrinoTask2
@trigger    OnLeaveNeutrinoRegion
@once

{@Radio} Looks like you’re drifting away from the cluster.

:: IncorrectSubmission
@trigger    OnIncorrectOpenIdSubmission

$call SubtitleController->SetSubtitlePosition(0.5, 1, 0, -140)
{@Radio} Hmm, that wasn’t correct, remember to look at your photometer, and then line it up with the closest range in your manual.
$call Wait(1)
$call SubtitleController->SetSubtitlePosition(0.5, 0, 0, 40)

:: FirstDupliacteSubmission
@trigger    OnDuplicateOpenIdSubmission
@boostScore 100
@cutscene
@once

{@Radio} Looks like you’ve already submitted that info. 
{@Radio} You won’t get any points towards your access level for identifying that property again.

:: DupliacteSubmission
@trigger    OnDuplicateOpenIdSubmission
@interrupt

{@Astrid} Looks like I have to determine the apparent magnitude of some of the other stars in this cluster. $[Astrid/L1/l1_a_18]

:: PointsUpdated
@trigger    PointsUpdated
@when   sciencePoints > 2
@boostScore 200
@interrupt
@cutscene
@once

$call SetInputState(false)
$call SetRefGuideActive(false)

$call Wait(3)
$call StopOpenMode()
$call ClearMonitorSelection()
{@Radio} You’ve identified the necessary data to earn a higher access level. 
// {@Dad} You’ll need to tune to the right frequency on your radio to unlock your equipment. $[Day1/Dad/l1_d_s34]

// $call HintModals->SlideInFromRight("RadioControls", 0.4) 

// $call Wait(1)

// $call HintModals->Hide("RadioControls", 0.2)

//TODO Seperate Node Here
$call MonitorUI->PlayRadioDownload(2)
$call Wait(1)
{@Radio} Ope, and I need to read this thing.... (*clears throat*) 
$call MonitorUI->ShowCeresLogo()
$call SetInstrumentUnlocked(ColorInstrument, true)
$call SetInstrumentUnlocked(TemperatureInstrument, true)
{@Radio} Congratulations on being awarded clearance level one. You are now cleared to use the color meter. $[Day1/Radio/l1_r_3]
{@Astrid} Starting at the bottom... clearance level one. $[Astrid/L1/l1_a_10]
{@Radio} Please reference your CERES Operator Manual for further information about your equipment.  $[Day1/Radio/l1_r_3(2)]
{@Radio} Thanking you for being an important part of the CERES Distributed Network of Citizen Observatories. Together, we will map the stars for a better tomorrow. $[Day1/Radio/l1_r_3(3)]

{@Astrid} Ugh, riviting... $[Astrid/L1/l1_a_11]

{@Radio} Tuning you to the Ice Cube CERES headquarters for further instruction... $[Day1/Radio/l1_r_4]
$call MonitorUI->HideCeresLogo()
$call Wait(1)

{@Astrid} (*Sigh*) ...Another birthday without Elijah. Maybe he’s watching the Perseids, wherever he is...  $[Astrid/L1/l1_a_12]
{@Astrid} I think I saw something about Perseus in that reference guide... $[Astrid/L1/l1_a_13]
//TODO
$call OpenRefGuidePage("DataTransfer")
{@Astrid} Huh… There’s something about Perseus here… $[Astrid/L1/l1_a_14]
{@Astrid} Aha! $[Astrid/L1/l1_a_15]
{@Astrid} Can this telescope can help me find Perseus? I hope I didn't miss the meteor shower. $[Astrid/L1/l1_a_16]
(*typing sounds*)
$call StartPuzzleNavigation()
$call SetInputState(true)

:: AnothaPoint
@trigger    PointsUpdated
@when   sciencePoints > 1
@interrupt
@cutscene
@once

{@Astrid} Okay, got it! $[Astrid/L1/l1_a_17]

:: FirstPoint
@trigger    PointsUpdated
@when   sciencePoints > 0
@interrupt
@cutscene
@once

$call SubtitleController->SetSubtitlePosition(0.5, 0, 0, 40)

:: HotColdEncouragement3
@trigger    OnConstellationNavWarmer
@when   newPips == 2
@once

{@Astrid} Warrmer...

:: HotColdEncouragement4
@trigger    OnConstellationNavWarmer
@when   newPips == 3
@once

{@Astrid} Warmer.

:: Colder3
@trigger    OnConstellationNavColder
@when   newPips == 1
@once

{@Astrid} Colder...

:: Colder4
@trigger    OnConstellationNavColder
@when   newPips == 2
@once

{@Astrid} Getting Colder...

:: PuzzleNavigationComplete
@trigger    PuzzleNavigationComplete
@boostScore 100
@cutscene
@once

$call SubtitleController->SetSubtitlePosition(0.5, 1, 0, -140)
$call StopPuzzleNavigation()
$call SetInputState(false)
$call SetRefGuideActive(false)
$call StartPuzzleMode()

{@Astrid} (*Wistful sigh*) Happy birthday to me. $[Astrid/L1/l1_a_20]
{@Astrid} Whoooaa... what's all this? $[Astrid/L1/l1_a_21]
{@Astrid} It must be the data from that Perseus page! $[Astrid/L1/l1_a_22]
{@Astrid} Do I finally get to do astronomy? I never thought this would happen. This is wild. $[Astrid/L1/l1_a_23] 
{@Astrid} Elijah is so far ahead of me. Well, here goes nothing! Aunt Martha would not be happy about this. $[Astrid/L1/l1_a_24]
{@Astrid} Okay, you got this Astrid… Start with what I know - the coordinates for Atik.  $[Astrid/L1/l1_a_25]

$set temp:waitingForSelectAtik = true
$call Wait(0.5)
$call HintModals->SlideInFromRight("FirstPuzzleStar", 0.4)
$call SetInputState(true)
$call SubtitleController->SetSubtitlePosition(0.5, 0, 0, 40)
$branch .SelectAtikReminder

:: SelectAtikReminder
$call Wait(10)
$if temp:waitingForSelectAtik
    {@Astrid}  It looks like the star compass gives me readings when I select the stars. That helps. $[Astrid/L1/l1_a_26]
    $goto .SelectAtikReminder
$endif

:: FirstPuzzleStarSelected
@trigger   OnStarSelected
@when   starName == "Atik", temp:waitingForSelectAtik
@boostScore 100
@interrupt
@cutscene
@once

$call LockMonitorFocus()
$set temp:waitingForSelectAppMag = true
$set temp:waitingForSelectAtik = false
$call HintModals->Hide("FirstPuzzleStar", 0.2)
$call SubtitleController->SetSubtitlePosition(0.5, 1, 0, -140)
$call IsolatePuzzleCell(1, 3)
{@Astrid} Okay, apparent magnitude… I can load that from the Photometer. $[Astrid/L1/l1_a_27]
$call Wait(1)
$call SubtitleController->SetSubtitlePosition(0.5, 0, 0, 40)

:: NotAtikAstrid
@trigger    OnPuzzleCellSelected
@when   cellId != "R1C3", temp:waitingForSelectAppMag

{@Astrid} I'm need the apparent magnitude space for Atik on this grid... $[Astrid/L1/l1_a_28]

:: AtikAppMagFilled
@trigger    OnPuzzleCellFilled
@when   cellId = "R1C3", temp:waitingForFillAppMag
@boostScore 100 
@cutscene
@interrupt
@once

$set temp:waitingForFillAppMag = false
$set temp:waitingForBlueFilter = true
$call UnlockMonitorFocus()
$call ReleaseIsolatedPuzzle()
$call SetInstrumentUnlocked(BlueWavelength, true)
$call SetInputState(false)
{@Astrid} Let's see... to fill in the rest of this sequence, I also need the blue magnitude.  $[Astrid/L1/l1_a_29]
{@Astrid} The blue wavelength filter is there on the moniter. $[Astrid/L1/l1_a_30]
$call SetRefGuidePagesLocked(false)
$call Wait(1)
$call SetInputState(true)

:: AtikBlueLightSelected
@trigger    OnPuzzleCellSelected
@when   cellId == "R1C4", temp:waitingForBlueLight
@interrupt
@once

$call ReleaseIsolatedPuzzle()

:: BlueFilterSelected
@trigger    OnLabInteraction
@when   actorId == "BlueFilter", temp:waitingForBlueFilter

$set temp:waitingForBlueFilter = false
$set temp:waitingForBlueLight = true
{@Astrid} Ok, now I can load this data into the blue magnitude space with my photometer just like before. $[Astrid/L1/l1_a_3]
$call IsolatePuzzleCell(1, 4)

:: AtikNotBlueFilterSelected
@trigger    OnLabInteraction
@when   actorId != "BlueFilter", cellId != "R1C4", temp:waitingForBlueFilter
@interrupt

{@Astrid} I need to select the blue wavelength filter just below the monitor. $[Astrid/L1/l1_a_34]

:: NotBlueLightAstrid
@trigger OnPuzzleCellSelected
@when   cellId != "R1C4", temp:waitingForBlueLight
@interrupt

{@Astrid} It looks like if I select the blue space on the identification grid then I can load it in from the photometer.

:: AtikBlueMagFilled
@trigger    OnPuzzleCellFilled
@when   cellId == "R1C4", temp:waitingForBlueLight
@cutscene
@once

$set temp:waitingForBlueLight = false
$call SetInputState(false)
$call ReleaseIsolatedPuzzle()
{@Astrid} It looks like I have the apparent magnitude of the star... and the blue magnitude. So now I can calculate it’s color index. $[Astrid/L1/l1_a_35] 
{@Astrid} The hotter the star, the bluer it is. Now I can input the color of the star... I can select the color space for Atik. $[Astrid/L1/l1_a_36]
$call IsolatePuzzleCell(1, 2)
$call SetInputState(true)
$set temp:waitingForFillColor = true

:: AtikColorCellSelected
@trigger    OnPuzzleCellSelected
@when   cellId == "R1C2", temp:waitingForFillColor

$call ReleaseIsolatedPuzzle()

:: AtikColorFilled
@trigger OnPuzzleCellFilled
@when   cellId == "R1C2", temp:waitingForFillColor
@interrupt
@cutscene
@once

$set temp:waitingForFillColor = false
{@Astrid} Now it’s just process of elimination. Start with your known info, and work your way through. Maybe the reference guide can help.
$call ReleaseIsolatedPuzzle()

:: AtikAppMagSelected
@trigger    OnPuzzleCellSelected
@when   cellId == "R1C3", temp:waitingForSelectAppMag
@cutscene
@interrupt
@once

$set temp:waitingForFillAppMag = true
$set temp:waitingForSelectAppMag = false
$call AddIsolatedSlot(ApparentMagnitude)
{@Astrid} Now all I have to do is load in data from the photometer.

:: AstridThatsNotThePhotometer
@trigger OnLabInteraction
@when actorId != "PhotometerLoadBtn", temp:waitingForSelectAppMag
{@Astrid} Now all I have to do is load in data from the photometer.

:: PuzzleGridReadyForSubmission
@trigger    OnPuzzleGridFullyPopulated
@cutscene
@once

{@Astrid} That’s all the data… (*deep breath*) Here goes nothing!

:: IncorrectPuzzleSubmission
@trigger    IncorrectPuzzleSubmission
@cutscene

{@Astrid} Hmm, looks like that wasn’t correct... $[Day1/Dad/l1_d_s32]

:: PerseusPuzzleComplete
@trigger    CorrectPuzzleSubmission
@when   puzzleName == "Perseus"
@cutscene
@interrupt
@once

$call StopPuzzleMode()
$call SetInputState(false)

$call Wait(2)
$call ClearMonitorSelection()
{@Elijah} If you’re hearing this… it means you didn’t give up. Good. Remember—Perseus didn’t wait for the gods to fix it. 
{@Elijah} He just did what had to be done. The satellite’s still up there, and maybe—just maybe—someone still believes it matters.

{@Astrid} Elijah! Its so good to hear a recording of his voice. Its been so long since I've gotten more than a letter. 
{@Dad} Ceres HQ checking in. Great work today!
{@Dad} It’s late where you are. Get some rest, kid. I sent you a letter. You should get it in a few weeks.
{@Astrid} (*yawns*) Ok. I’ll be looking out for it. Can I say I miss you on here?
{@Dad} (*half-sigh half-laugh*) Over and out, Little Bear.
$call Wait(1)

$call EndDay2->BeginCutscene()
$call Wait(1)
{@Astrid} Huh... What are you getting yourself into, Elijah?
$call Wait(1)

:: EndDay
@trigger    CutsceneEnd
@when cutsceneId == "EndDay2"
@who    Radio

$call LoadNextDay()